abstract: >-
  Maple worksheets, a Julia solver and computed spectra for the quasinormal modes of the Kazakov–Solodukhin
  quantum-corrected black hole, in the minimally and conformally coupled scalar sectors, the electromagnetic sector
  and an axial effective-source Regge–Wheeler sector. The radial problem is reduced by a Chebyshev collocation to a
  quadratic matrix pencil, assembled with 200 decimal digits and solved with 220 digits at three resolutions, and only
  the roots on which the three resolutions agree are kept; 141 tables of modes are included.
